# Files and folders that chezmoi deletes from your home folder when it applies
# the dotfiles, if they exist. Each line is a path in your home folder, written
# without the ~/. (This file is read as a template, like .chezmoiignore.)
#
# chezmoi stops managing a file that is deleted from this repository, but it
# leaves the copy that is already in your home folder. Listing the file here
# deletes that copy too, on every machine's next `chezmoi update`.

# fish files these dotfiles no longer ship, so that fish's own behaviour comes
# back everywhere: fish_user_key_bindings.fish replaced what Up and Down do, and
# help.fish replaced fish's own help command. To put your own file at one of
# these paths later, delete its line here first, or chezmoi deletes the file
# again on every apply.
.config/fish/functions/fish_user_key_bindings.fish
.config/fish/functions/help.fish
